# .windsurfrules — CodeTrust AI Governance for Windsurf IDE
#
# These rules are enforced by CodeTrust's governance stack:
# Layer 1: These instructions (advisory — agent compliance expected)
# Layer 2: VS Code extension on-save scanning (automatic)
# Layer 3: Pre-commit hook (blocks bad code at commit time)
# Layer 4: CI/CD GitHub Action (blocks bad code at merge time)

## MANDATORY: Gateway Proxy Enforcement

Before ANY terminal command:
1. Call mcp_codetrust-gat_codetrust_validate_command with the command
2. If status is BLOCKED → do NOT run the command, use the safe alternative
3. If status is APPROVED → proceed

Before writing ANY file:
1. Call mcp_codetrust-gat_codetrust_validate_file_write with the file path
2. If BLOCKED → stop

Before installing ANY package:
1. Call mcp_codetrust-gat_codetrust_validate_package
2. If BLOCKED → do not install

## MANDATORY: Code Quality Scanning

Before writing ANY code:
1. Call codetrust_pre_action with a description of what you plan to do
2. If verdict is BLOCK → stop and fix the plan
3. If verdict is WARN → acknowledge each warning

After writing or modifying ANY file:
1. Call codetrust_static_scan on every file you changed
2. Call codetrust_deep_scan if you created new files or modified imports
3. Call codetrust_hallucination_scan if you wrote new security-sensitive code
4. If any finding has severity BLOCK → fix immediately
5. If any finding has severity WARN → fix or explain

Before committing:
1. Call codetrust_post_action with repo root and list of changed files
2. All BLOCK findings must be resolved — zero tolerance

## Absolute Prohibitions

These are enforced by the pre-commit hook regardless of agent compliance:

- No eval() or exec() with user input
- No hardcoded secrets (use environment variables)
- No heredocs (use file creation tools)
- No pickle.load with untrusted data
- No SQL string formatting (use parameterized queries)
- No print() — use structlog
- No wildcard imports
- No bare except:
- No Any types
- No mutable default arguments
- Never run git push — user pushes manually

## Quality Standards

- Every function has type annotations
- Every public function has a docstring
- Max 40 lines per function
- All external HTTP calls wrapped in try/except with timeout
- All Pydantic models use strict=True
